WEBVTT

00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:11.940
Are you still awake?

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:13.500
I was just about to sleep.

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:16.280
Okay. Well, I'm heading to work.

00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:17.730
Have a safe trip.

00:00:17.730 --> 00:00:18.910
Good night.

00:00:24.070 --> 00:00:25.540
I've got snacks, too.

00:00:27.530 --> 00:00:29.670
Let me put some fresh tea out.

00:00:37.310 --> 00:00:38.690
That was cool!

00:00:38.690 --> 00:00:40.260
What was?

00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:41.560
Just now.

00:00:55.150 --> 00:00:56.840
I'm sorry...

00:00:56.840 --> 00:00:58.780
It's okay.

00:01:13.770 --> 00:01:16.670
Grandma, can you do it again?

00:01:16.670 --> 00:01:18.350
You're a silly girl.

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:25.770
Again!

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:28.560
Oh my... what a waste of tea.

00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:34.300
Now, when you're nervous, 
your movements can get clunky,

00:01:34.300 --> 00:01:37.790
so we're going to practice just 
getting up and sitting down.

00:01:38.450 --> 00:01:42.510
Note the difference between standing 
right up and standing up slowly.

00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:45.460
That was standing straight up.

00:01:45.460 --> 00:01:47.690
Slowly, it's more like this.

00:01:48.230 --> 00:01:50.170
You lean over first, and then stand.

00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:54.000
Do you understand the difference? 
Then let's try it.

00:02:01.130 --> 00:02:03.060
Ow!

00:02:22.450 --> 00:02:23.950
Tsubame?

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:30.180
Okay, step, step, step.

00:02:30.670 --> 00:02:32.420
You want to have your hands out
 and your chest up,

00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:35.750
walking along a straight line. 
That's the pretty way to do it.

00:02:36.110 --> 00:02:39.410
Motohashi, your head's swinging 
a bit too much from side to side.

00:02:39.410 --> 00:02:41.950
Try to walk in a straight line.

00:02:41.950 --> 00:02:45.760
It might be easier to sway like that,
 but does not look as nice.

00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:48.480
Yamashiro, your head is moving, too.

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:58.130
Now, with a model's walk, your 
legs cross in front of you,

00:02:58.130 --> 00:03:01.150
so even if your hips swing, 
your head has to stay steady.

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:07.700
<i>So there you have it. The bottom line is...</i>

00:03:08.650 --> 00:03:10.420
<i>Maeda did it!</i>

00:03:14.220 --> 00:03:15.990
<i>Maeda did it!</i>

00:03:26.010 --> 00:03:27.220
I did it!

00:03:33.020 --> 00:03:36.170
I'm not sure you're strong 
enough to help, honey.

00:03:36.170 --> 00:03:37.520
Try leaning over more!

00:03:37.960 --> 00:03:39.900
So that your head is this far down.

00:03:40.730 --> 00:03:44.370
Wouldn't I fall over if I did that?

00:03:44.370 --> 00:03:45.860
Look at this!

00:03:45.860 --> 00:03:47.490
Oh, this is impressive.

00:03:47.490 --> 00:03:51.170
You lean down like that, and then when 
your behind goes up, you straighten!

00:03:52.220 --> 00:03:53.700
Like, bam, bam!

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:54.170
Bam...

00:03:55.250 --> 00:03:56.110
Bam.

00:03:56.780 --> 00:03:58.870
See! You were able to stand!

00:03:58.870 --> 00:03:59.710
Wow...

00:03:59.710 --> 00:04:05.350
Left, right, left, right...

00:04:05.350 --> 00:04:07.220
You can sway all you want, okay?

00:04:07.220 --> 00:04:09.850
You've got a knack for this, Tsubame.

00:04:09.850 --> 00:04:12.740
When you go to the left, 
it pulls your right leg along,

00:04:12.740 --> 00:04:15.260
and then to the right, with your left leg.

00:04:15.260 --> 00:04:17.230
It's totally natural, and should be easier!

00:04:35.900 --> 00:04:36.750
Okay!

00:04:39.550 --> 00:04:42.970
<b><i>Episode 7        I Have To Do It For Myself!</i></b>

00:05:36.180 --> 00:05:37.330
<b><i>Keep</i></b>

00:05:38.600 --> 00:05:39.710
<b><i>Your</i></b>

00:05:41.230 --> 00:05:42.250
<b><i>Hands</i></b>

00:05:43.650 --> 00:05:44.630
<b><i>Off</i></b>

00:05:44.960 --> 00:05:55.620
<b><i>Keep Your Hands Off Eizouken!</i></b>

00:05:55.620 --> 00:06:03.830
<b><i>Keep Your Hands Off Eizouken!</i></b>

00:06:09.970 --> 00:06:12.510
<b>Student Council</b>

00:06:09.970 --> 00:06:12.510
<b>Motor Vehicle Club</b>

00:06:13.710 --> 00:06:15.220
Thanks for the lift!

00:06:15.980 --> 00:06:19.060
I'm going to unload this stuff, 
so it'll just be a minute.

00:06:22.570 --> 00:06:25.330
Huh, this one says, "Eating bread crusts."

00:06:22.910 --> 00:06:24.430
That ought to do it.

00:06:25.330 --> 00:06:27.650
This one is the sound for 
eating a croissant...

00:06:27.650 --> 00:06:29.420
Hey, stop that!

00:06:29.420 --> 00:06:31.950
Get that stuff unpacked, and then get in here!

00:06:32.500 --> 00:06:34.810
We need to have a sound meeting.

00:06:35.890 --> 00:06:37.160
Right.

00:06:40.580 --> 00:06:42.740
I think I get what you're going for.

00:06:43.530 --> 00:06:46.760
I'll look into how the sounds for 
monsters and robots are done.

00:06:47.300 --> 00:06:50.710
But in terms of specific sounds 
that will match your footage,

00:06:50.710 --> 00:06:52.540
even for the more mundane scenes,

00:06:52.540 --> 00:06:55.760
it's hard to know what'll be needed
without seeing what you're dealing with.

00:06:55.760 --> 00:06:58.970
And it'll be really tough to set 
you up without knowing the timing.

00:06:59.560 --> 00:07:01.020
I see.

00:07:01.020 --> 00:07:04.300
The dialog will also have to be 
balanced against the rest of the sound,

00:07:04.300 --> 00:07:07.570
so if I knew the timing and volume 
you wanted, it'd be easier to figure out.

00:07:07.570 --> 00:07:09.370
There are also the things 
that affect acoustics,

00:07:09.370 --> 00:07:11.490
like the size of the location and its layout,

00:07:11.490 --> 00:07:14.250
so even if it's just a broad outline,
 that'd be handy to know.

00:07:14.250 --> 00:07:17.580
Understood. We'll get the dialog 
recorded as soon as we can.

00:07:17.580 --> 00:07:19.750
That means it's time for edits.

00:07:19.750 --> 00:07:22.270
Should we make a video out of the storyboard?

00:07:22.890 --> 00:07:24.890
That way we can set the 
timing up for the sounds.

00:07:24.890 --> 00:07:28.010
The timing is hard to guess at 
until it's actually animated...

00:07:28.010 --> 00:07:30.140
But it needs to be done to 
get the sound ready in time,

00:07:30.140 --> 00:07:31.470
so I'll figure something out!

00:07:31.470 --> 00:07:33.340
How are we going to handle casting, anyway?

00:07:33.340 --> 00:07:36.930
It's actually been settled already.

00:07:37.890 --> 00:07:40.210
The client has demands.

00:07:41.250 --> 00:07:45.580
<b>Team</b>

00:07:45.560 --> 00:07:47.980
<b>Darker than the last cut
\h\h\h\h\h\h(but the power is still on)
\h\h\h\h\h\h Monitor is lit brightly</b>

00:07:45.580 --> 00:07:47.790
<b>Officer A</b>

00:07:45.580 --> 00:07:47.980
There have been reports of 
vibrations being detected underground!

00:07:47.980 --> 00:07:49.990
<b>Voice on the Radio:
"It's a monster.
 A crab-type monster
 has appeared!"</b>

00:07:47.980 --> 00:07:49.990
It's a monster. A crab-type 
monster has appeared.

00:07:49.990 --> 00:07:53.030
Time to blast out of the water!

00:07:54.740 --> 00:07:58.750
Launch it from the catapult!

00:07:58.750 --> 00:08:00.050
Cut!

00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:03.730
Your ad-libs are things that 
will be conveyed in the footage,

00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:10.460
<b>Robot VS Monster (TBD)
Voice Over Script</b>

00:08:03.730 --> 00:08:05.870
so you don't have to describe every moment.

00:08:05.870 --> 00:08:08.410
And you don't have to 
vocalize the sound effects.

00:08:08.410 --> 00:08:10.460
They'll overlap everyone else's dialog.

00:08:11.010 --> 00:08:13.770
I think we'd be better off 
recording Seki and Goto's dialog

00:08:13.770 --> 00:08:15.560
for cuts 12 through 21 separately.

00:08:15.560 --> 00:08:16.850
Sorry about that!

00:08:16.850 --> 00:08:19.750
Pile bunker!

00:08:18.380 --> 00:08:20.780
We are honestly so excited about this!

00:08:19.750 --> 00:08:23.460
Recoil start!

00:08:22.140 --> 00:08:24.500
Can we adjust the volume differently per actor?

00:08:24.500 --> 00:08:25.940
Of course.

00:08:25.940 --> 00:08:29.100
But we need that storyboard 
video for him to practice with,

00:08:29.100 --> 00:08:32.170
or it's going to be really hard to get 
him to match the timing of the animation.

00:08:51.170 --> 00:08:55.630
<b>Film</b>

00:08:52.660 --> 00:08:55.650
Wait, the song for the 
opening still isn't ready?

00:08:55.650 --> 00:08:57.050
Not only is it not ready,

00:08:57.050 --> 00:09:01.220
there was so much trouble putting it 
together that they said to forget about it.

00:09:01.220 --> 00:09:03.810
Which means less work for us, thankfully.

00:09:03.810 --> 00:09:07.940
If there's no opening, I kind 
like the idea of just—boom!

00:09:07.940 --> 00:09:09.560
Chomp, chomp!

00:09:09.560 --> 00:09:12.770
And starting with the monster showing up.

00:09:13.940 --> 00:09:15.510
Mizusaki, how about the music?

00:09:16.300 --> 00:09:18.440
I forgot! Let me ask now!

00:09:18.440 --> 00:09:20.280
We'll use something from a free music library.

00:09:20.280 --> 00:09:22.570
Doumeki, can you look into it?

00:09:22.570 --> 00:09:25.190
Uh, sure. I can try.

00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:27.710
Excuse us.

00:09:27.710 --> 00:09:29.810
Oh, wow, nice.

00:09:31.650 --> 00:09:32.710
U-Um...

00:09:33.170 --> 00:09:37.930
About the sun, this would be the west, 
which would make this a sunset...

00:09:37.930 --> 00:09:39.730
I was hoping it could be consistent.

00:09:41.140 --> 00:09:43.100
I mean, is it really a problem?

00:09:43.100 --> 00:09:45.080
W-Well, I think...

00:09:45.080 --> 00:09:49.450
Since it's an actual location, and 
changes the connotation of the camera pan...

00:09:50.980 --> 00:09:53.260
Uh, the car here was supposed 
to be drawn as a cel.

00:09:53.260 --> 00:09:56.220
It looked a little barren, 
composition-wise, without it.

00:09:56.990 --> 00:09:58.430
But the cels will be animated,

00:09:58.430 --> 00:10:00.370
so if it's in the background too,
 there'll be two of them.

00:10:01.430 --> 00:10:02.970
So is it not gonna work?

00:10:02.970 --> 00:10:05.570
If we erase the car...

00:10:05.570 --> 00:10:07.460
Huh, that doesn't look right.

00:10:09.250 --> 00:10:11.270
Did you cut the image board out for this?

00:10:11.270 --> 00:10:15.170
Oh, I see. You copied Asakusa's 
board and then stuck it on there.

00:10:15.170 --> 00:10:15.940
Is that a problem?

00:10:15.940 --> 00:10:18.970
It's just kind of blurry...

00:10:18.970 --> 00:10:20.460
And the texture is...

00:10:20.460 --> 00:10:22.170
Wait, is this line right?

00:10:23.180 --> 00:10:25.300
A character's supposed to pop out from there.

00:10:26.660 --> 00:10:30.520
I made it so the light was 
shining down, like you said.

00:10:30.520 --> 00:10:32.270
Pretty good, right?

00:10:32.270 --> 00:10:35.070
Or isn't it? That's what you asked for, right?

00:10:35.070 --> 00:10:37.750
It's just... it's turning 
into a different film...

00:10:39.050 --> 00:10:40.990
Oh, this isn't gonna work!

00:10:41.990 --> 00:10:46.580
But Asakusa, you said the 
details were up to me, right?

00:10:46.580 --> 00:10:49.060
Yes, but while following the image board,

00:10:49.060 --> 00:10:53.060
and keeping the layout lines in mind.

00:10:54.370 --> 00:10:56.930
This sounds different from what 
you were asking about before.

00:10:56.930 --> 00:10:58.460
So there's no room for expression?

00:10:58.460 --> 00:10:59.280
Hey...

00:10:59.280 --> 00:11:02.730
Um, let me know if there's 
anything else that needs fixing.

00:11:02.730 --> 00:11:05.190
I can adjust it digitally.

00:11:05.190 --> 00:11:06.440
You're gonna change it?!

00:11:06.440 --> 00:11:09.890
Just making a few changes 
to the general look!

00:11:09.890 --> 00:11:12.770
S-Sure. That'd be a big help.

00:11:13.400 --> 00:11:17.970
I like that Kubo girl. 
She's willing to make corrections.

00:11:17.970 --> 00:11:21.210
That should help take care of some of it.

00:11:21.690 --> 00:11:24.120
That said...

00:11:25.130 --> 00:11:28.010
You didn't need to take over all of these!

00:11:28.010 --> 00:11:31.270
Doing it myself is faster than 
explaining how to fix it.

00:11:31.270 --> 00:11:35.700
A director needs to be able to give 
directions to other artists.

00:11:35.700 --> 00:11:37.650
You're supposed to be helping with animation,

00:11:37.650 --> 00:11:38.740
and handling the photography,

00:11:38.740 --> 00:11:40.970
on top of the edit!

00:11:40.970 --> 00:11:45.180
I get how she feels, though. 
It's just faster to redraw it yourself.

00:11:46.600 --> 00:11:47.930
You do realize that

00:11:47.930 --> 00:11:51.390
our delays are due to being behind 
schedule with animation, yes?

00:11:51.390 --> 00:11:54.290
The PC room where the animation needs 
to be done won't be free forever.

00:11:54.290 --> 00:11:58.560
If you don't get in there soon, 
you won't finish all the art we need.

00:11:58.560 --> 00:12:01.040
For the record, if we fall any further behind,

00:12:01.040 --> 00:12:03.600
the dozens of cuts you have 
cooking in that tablet

00:12:03.600 --> 00:12:05.280
are never going to see the light of day.

00:12:05.280 --> 00:12:05.920
No way!

00:12:05.920 --> 00:12:07.490
I'm gonna draw it all!

00:12:13.460 --> 00:12:15.250
And with that being the case...

00:12:16.170 --> 00:12:17.910
All right, we'll continue next time.

00:12:18.500 --> 00:12:19.760
Time to chow down!

00:12:20.170 --> 00:12:21.890
Let's sit somewhere we can see the lightning.

00:12:22.990 --> 00:12:25.230
I'm gonna work on this a bit more...

00:12:26.050 --> 00:12:27.930
I guess I should work on the backgrounds.

00:12:28.740 --> 00:12:31.030
<i>Uh, we have a bit of news.</i>

00:12:31.030 --> 00:12:33.270
<i>There's a warning for torrential rain,</i>

00:12:33.270 --> 00:12:34.850
<i>so classes are canceled for the rest of the day.</i>

00:12:35.660 --> 00:12:38.490
<i>All students are to head 
home as quickly as possible.</i>

00:12:39.330 --> 00:12:41.040
With the amount of work we have to do,

00:12:41.040 --> 00:12:43.350
we can't just take the rest of the day off.

00:12:43.350 --> 00:12:45.820
What do you think will happen to the 
food they had ready for lunch?

00:12:45.820 --> 00:12:46.990
It's raining!

00:12:46.990 --> 00:12:49.450
At times like this, 
you shouldn't be caught without...

00:12:49.450 --> 00:12:51.200
A rain poncho!

00:12:49.450 --> 00:12:51.200
<b>Rain Coat</b>

00:12:49.450 --> 00:12:51.200
<b>Super Durable</b>

00:12:52.420 --> 00:12:53.780
Evasive maneuvers!

00:12:59.090 --> 00:13:02.210
Since we've got our gym clothes, you want
 to hang out until the rain stops?

00:13:02.210 --> 00:13:03.530
Ugh, I'm freezing!

00:13:04.420 --> 00:13:13.180
<b>Please use the
 actual entrance</b>

00:13:05.030 --> 00:13:07.980
I'm going to use the bathhouse 
before heading home.

00:13:07.980 --> 00:13:12.090
A bathhouse?! I've never been to one before!

00:13:12.090 --> 00:13:13.180
I'm going, too!

00:13:13.570 --> 00:13:15.780
One sec, gotta notify Mom.

00:13:16.250 --> 00:13:19.740
Hey, it's me. Can I stop by the 
bathhouse before going home?

00:13:18.500 --> 00:13:20.920
Are Asakusa's parents strict or something?

00:13:20.920 --> 00:13:22.730
With Kanamori and Mizusaki.

00:13:21.170 --> 00:13:23.730
It's just a matter of keeping them informed.

00:13:22.730 --> 00:13:25.470
Class let out early because 
of the rain warning.

00:13:23.740 --> 00:13:26.060
As long as she keeps in touch,
 they won't be upset.

00:13:26.060 --> 00:13:29.250
Huh, that's not like my parents at all.

00:13:30.940 --> 00:13:32.120
She said it's okay!

00:13:32.120 --> 00:13:36.120
<b>Please use the
 actual entrance</b>

00:13:39.130 --> 00:13:41.420
<b>Ongyoku Bathhouse</b>

00:13:41.420 --> 00:13:43.670
<b>Ongyoku Bathhouse</b>

00:13:42.370 --> 00:13:43.670
Oh.

00:13:43.670 --> 00:13:45.520
We had to take the indoor route.

00:13:43.670 --> 00:13:52.560
<b>Reception</b>

00:13:45.520 --> 00:13:47.540
Must be rough out in that rain.

00:13:47.540 --> 00:13:49.090
Three students.

00:13:47.550 --> 00:13:48.580
Huh, wooden plates.

00:13:48.580 --> 00:13:50.470
When you take them, they lock.

00:13:49.530 --> 00:13:51.570
Enjoying some fun with your friends today?

00:13:51.570 --> 00:13:52.560
No.

00:13:52.560 --> 00:13:54.270
Enjoy yourselves!

00:13:52.560 --> 00:13:54.270
<b>Sponge</b>

00:13:54.270 --> 00:13:56.900
Kanamori, what is this thing?

00:13:54.270 --> 00:13:58.560
<b>Gentlemen</b>

00:13:54.270 --> 00:13:58.560
<b>Ladies</b>

00:13:56.900 --> 00:13:58.560
The key for your locker.

00:13:58.560 --> 00:14:00.690
You pull here to get the key to come out.

00:14:00.690 --> 00:14:02.150
That's adorable!

00:14:02.150 --> 00:14:03.490
"Ladies"!

00:14:02.150 --> 00:14:07.740
<b>Ladies</b>

00:14:03.490 --> 00:14:05.980
The "ladies" curtain that's so famous!

00:14:09.420 --> 00:14:11.660
You put your clothes in here? That's neat!

00:14:12.100 --> 00:14:14.610
Do you think they'd mind 
if I took pictures inside?

00:14:14.610 --> 00:14:16.750
They sure as hell would!

00:14:19.540 --> 00:14:21.310
So I can jump in here?

00:14:21.310 --> 00:14:23.190
That's the rinsing water.

00:14:24.050 --> 00:14:25.760
You're supposed to wash off first.

00:14:25.760 --> 00:14:32.470
<b>Rules for the Bathhouse</b>

00:14:26.070 --> 00:14:29.380
You'll see rules along those lines 
in just about any bathhouse.

00:14:29.380 --> 00:14:30.610
Like a tutorial...

00:14:30.610 --> 00:14:31.690
Check this out!

00:14:32.470 --> 00:14:34.560
A bucket in each hand!

00:14:34.560 --> 00:14:36.730
I have all I need to clean 
off in one fell swoop!

00:14:38.650 --> 00:14:42.730
You're trying to save water when 
you paid to bathe in a bathhouse?!

00:14:42.730 --> 00:14:44.480
Stop showing off!

00:14:46.230 --> 00:14:47.820
Kanamori, could you do that again?

00:14:50.530 --> 00:14:51.820
One more time!

00:14:54.590 --> 00:14:55.830
One more time!

00:14:59.080 --> 00:15:01.250
Enough already!

00:15:03.250 --> 00:15:05.530
Sorry! The movement of the water was just...

00:15:05.530 --> 00:15:07.230
Can it! And take this!

00:15:09.490 --> 00:15:10.790
By the way, Mizusaki,

00:15:10.790 --> 00:15:13.020
will your parents be mad about 
your clothes getting soaked?

00:15:13.020 --> 00:15:16.010
Nah. My parents give me a lot of freedom.

00:15:16.010 --> 00:15:17.710
The only times I can 
remember them being mad...

00:15:18.250 --> 00:15:22.490
is when I tried to push the house with 
a car in preschool and broke a wall.

00:15:22.490 --> 00:15:25.680
And when I tried hatch an egg, 
but it rotted instead.

00:15:25.680 --> 00:15:27.320
The egg thing! I did that, too.

00:15:27.760 --> 00:15:30.320
They said we couldn't have an ostrich as a pet.

00:15:30.320 --> 00:15:31.210
An ostrich egg?!

00:15:31.900 --> 00:15:34.960
I tried to raise pigs for meat once.

00:15:34.960 --> 00:15:35.950
Who does that?!

00:15:36.310 --> 00:15:39.960
You know, other than forbidding anime,

00:15:39.960 --> 00:15:41.330
your parents seem pretty lenient, Mizusaki.

00:15:42.700 --> 00:15:46.380
Yeah. They generally let me do what I want.

00:15:46.730 --> 00:15:48.470
I think this stuff about me being an actress

00:15:48.470 --> 00:15:52.340
is my dad's idea of trying to 
make my mom's dream come true.

00:15:52.340 --> 00:15:54.540
And your mother doesn't care?

00:15:54.540 --> 00:15:56.760
She totally lets me have my freedom.

00:15:56.760 --> 00:16:00.020
I'm more of a grandma's girl, anyway.

00:16:30.510 --> 00:16:32.510
An impenetrable barrier!

00:16:32.510 --> 00:16:33.810
A barrier...

00:16:34.510 --> 00:16:36.110
You're pretty tough.

00:16:36.530 --> 00:16:37.930
Right back at you.

00:16:37.930 --> 00:16:40.180
Huh? Kanamori, are you getting out already?

00:16:40.770 --> 00:16:43.640
I haven't eaten yet.

00:16:43.660 --> 00:16:46.150
Dining Hall

00:16:44.450 --> 00:16:46.150
Dibs on the window seat!

00:16:47.050 --> 00:16:47.980
Huh...

00:16:47.980 --> 00:16:48.820
Look at this!

00:16:48.170 --> 00:16:49.690
m 170 111 l 174 212 506 202 499 192 521 182 522 142 508 134 505 114

00:16:48.170 --> 00:16:49.690
American
<b> All the Red Crawfish You Can Catch</b>

00:16:48.170 --> 00:16:49.690
600 Yen per person

00:16:48.170 --> 00:16:49.690
• You can eat any crawfish you catch!
• Boiling and deep frying
 on the house!

00:16:50.940 --> 00:16:53.030
What a wonderful setup.

00:16:53.030 --> 00:16:54.570
Got one! We got one!

00:16:57.160 --> 00:16:58.250
These are the ones we caught?

00:16:58.250 --> 00:17:01.470
I'd wager they make them purge 
 mud for a good long while,

00:17:01.470 --> 00:17:04.240
so the ones we caught will go to someone else.

00:17:04.240 --> 00:17:06.500
We should've marked them!

00:17:06.500 --> 00:17:08.590
I'll add a note to the bathhouse log.

00:17:08.610 --> 00:17:12.070
Dining Hall

00:17:26.690 --> 00:17:29.520
A specially made paddle boat for hot water!

00:18:11.930 --> 00:18:14.400
Hey, the rain's stopped.

00:18:14.400 --> 00:18:15.930
We should head home.

00:18:15.930 --> 00:18:17.020
I guess so.

00:18:19.030 --> 00:18:20.500
Asakusa isn't waking up.

00:18:20.500 --> 00:18:21.240
Leave her.

00:18:21.240 --> 00:18:23.030
We have to take her back with us...

00:18:23.660 --> 00:18:25.820
Asakusa!

00:18:27.040 --> 00:18:29.500
No good. Guess I'm carrying her.

00:18:30.190 --> 00:18:32.500
Upsy-daisy...

00:18:32.500 --> 00:18:34.500
<b>Ongyoku Bathhouse</b>

00:18:33.470 --> 00:18:34.500
Thanks.

00:18:37.510 --> 00:18:39.380
People are heavy.

00:18:39.380 --> 00:18:42.220
Her bag is stupidly heavy, too.

00:18:43.580 --> 00:18:45.100
Not lost...

00:18:45.100 --> 00:18:46.430
Did you wake up?

00:18:46.430 --> 00:18:47.730
Exploring...

00:18:50.560 --> 00:18:52.310
<b>Culture</b>

00:18:50.560 --> 00:18:52.310
<b>High School</b>

00:18:54.030 --> 00:18:56.110
And... then...

00:18:59.660 --> 00:19:01.280
Blargh!

00:19:02.850 --> 00:19:04.180
Pull yourself together!

00:19:04.180 --> 00:19:05.950
What's wrong, Mizusaki?

00:19:05.950 --> 00:19:09.490
Well, it's about the chainsaw's movement...

00:19:09.490 --> 00:19:13.170
I didn't want it to just breeze 
by like "bzzzt" and "shwooom"

00:19:13.170 --> 00:19:17.640
but more like... grind, grind, crunch, crunch, 
with rocks flying around and stuff,

00:19:17.640 --> 00:19:19.270
but I can't get it right.

00:19:20.190 --> 00:19:22.410
What about making the screen pan around?

00:19:22.410 --> 00:19:23.740
I thought about that!

00:19:23.740 --> 00:19:28.580
But then it makes the movement of the 
treads more smooth, and less impactful.

00:19:30.290 --> 00:19:32.010
Come on over, Kanamori.

00:19:32.830 --> 00:19:34.690
How am I supposed to be able to help?

00:19:35.000 --> 00:19:39.910
There you go again. Isn't a producer 
supposed to develop a discerning eye?

00:19:40.570 --> 00:19:42.100
Fair enough.

00:19:42.380 --> 00:19:44.120
<b>I just won an argument</b>

00:19:42.380 --> 00:19:44.120
<b>with Kanamori</b>

00:19:45.590 --> 00:19:51.110
To be honest, I can't imagine 
what else you might want to add.

00:19:51.110 --> 00:19:53.980
The big movements are satisfying to look at,

00:19:53.980 --> 00:19:57.340
so I don't see a problem with 
just going with what you have.

00:19:57.790 --> 00:19:59.540
I dunno.

00:19:59.540 --> 00:20:01.670
Let's try adding sound to it.

00:20:01.670 --> 00:20:03.690
As it is?

00:20:03.690 --> 00:20:06.040
It changes the whole feel it gives off.

00:20:06.040 --> 00:20:07.260
She's right.

00:20:07.260 --> 00:20:11.660
Animation otaku go as far as to mute 
the sound when they look at something.

00:20:30.120 --> 00:20:33.670
It definitely helps convey 
the impression of movement.

00:20:33.670 --> 00:20:35.620
A technique unto itself.

00:20:35.620 --> 00:20:38.780
Having proper sound takes some 
of the burden off an animator.

00:20:38.780 --> 00:20:41.150
I... I hate to admit it, though!

00:20:41.150 --> 00:20:44.010
You do realize film basically 
consists of images <i>and</i> sound, right?

00:20:44.010 --> 00:20:46.380
Have you considered that your vision for animation

00:20:46.380 --> 00:20:49.150
is too technical for people 
to understand, Mizusaki?

00:20:49.150 --> 00:20:53.600
But the people who can understand do,
 y'know? Everyone does it.

00:20:54.060 --> 00:20:58.360
Think about how pretty it is when 
a goldfish's tail is fluttering.

00:20:59.030 --> 00:21:00.990
Or swirls of cherry blossom petals...

00:21:02.140 --> 00:21:05.660
Dancing, too! That's all 
a performance of motion!

00:21:05.660 --> 00:21:07.910
And anime is another way to appreciate movement?

00:21:07.910 --> 00:21:10.820
I'd say it's the best way to appreciate it!

00:21:10.820 --> 00:21:13.980
Certainly, considering that 
every single motion is something

00:21:13.980 --> 00:21:15.420
intentionally depicted by an artist.

00:21:15.420 --> 00:21:18.300
It can be a pretty subtle movement, 
without a lot of exaggeration,

00:21:18.300 --> 00:21:21.420
but the fact that someone 
had to draw it out

00:21:21.420 --> 00:21:23.630
in order to make it move 
gives it a bigger impact.

00:21:23.630 --> 00:21:26.090
That's the big difference 
from live action.

00:21:26.090 --> 00:21:29.770
Think about a rocket. The rocket 
itself isn't the cool part.

00:21:29.770 --> 00:21:31.070
Yes, it is!

00:21:31.070 --> 00:21:32.490
Well, yeah, but what I'm saying is...

00:21:32.490 --> 00:21:35.480
The trail and clouds of smoke it gives off
 are all part of why it's cool!

00:21:35.480 --> 00:21:36.810
Exactly!

00:21:36.810 --> 00:21:39.020
Which is why this won't cut it!

00:21:39.020 --> 00:21:40.580
You want a long shot, like this!

00:21:40.580 --> 00:21:41.440
Then a close-up!

00:21:43.950 --> 00:21:45.490
And then the... uh...

00:21:45.490 --> 00:21:46.710
The nozzle's skirt.

00:21:45.490 --> 00:21:48.280
<b>Mizu</b>

00:21:46.710 --> 00:21:48.280
<b>Asa</b>

00:21:46.710 --> 00:21:48.280
You see that vibrate!

00:21:47.630 --> 00:21:48.280
<b>Kana</b>

00:21:48.280 --> 00:21:50.420
You see all of this white 
smoke coming from the rocket,

00:21:50.420 --> 00:21:52.450
spreading and billowing outwards,

00:21:52.450 --> 00:21:55.500
and depending on the location, 
it shakes like it's a solid shape!

00:21:55.500 --> 00:21:59.670
A big portion of the white smoke 
near the launchpad is actually steam

00:21:59.670 --> 00:22:03.230
that was vaporized by the rocket as part 
of the water sound suppression system.

00:22:03.230 --> 00:22:05.090
The water sound suppression 
system being—

00:22:05.090 --> 00:22:06.220
Stop.

00:22:07.550 --> 00:22:09.220
The shake of the security camera!

00:22:12.900 --> 00:22:13.830
And as it starts to tilt,

00:22:13.830 --> 00:22:16.730
the angle of the rocket and its 
exhaust stop being vertical!

00:22:16.730 --> 00:22:18.860
The tilt is a big deal.

00:22:18.860 --> 00:22:20.940
It continues to expel smoke!

00:22:23.440 --> 00:22:25.890
"This is the coolest part of a rocket!"

00:22:25.890 --> 00:22:28.110
You've got to make the art 
give that kind of feeling!

00:22:28.110 --> 00:22:30.570
Then it's like, "Yeah, you really get it!"

00:22:30.570 --> 00:22:32.550
"I don't know who you are, or where you are,"

00:22:32.550 --> 00:22:35.750
"but I appreciate your attention to detail!"

00:22:35.750 --> 00:22:38.850
That's why I want to make animation.

00:22:38.850 --> 00:22:42.020
As unpleasant as I find artistic passion,
 I think I grasp the concept.

00:22:43.070 --> 00:22:46.960
Would you prefer if I said, "I want to 
make lots of people smile with my anime!"?

00:22:46.960 --> 00:22:49.340
That would actually be more gross, yes.

00:22:49.940 --> 00:22:52.230
I think I'm starting to get you, Kanamori!

00:22:52.650 --> 00:22:55.590
<i>You have to draw the greatest world 
you imagine yourself, after all.</i>

00:22:56.100 --> 00:22:59.580
So, Mizusaki, you don't want to make anime,

00:22:59.580 --> 00:23:02.480
but are more concerned with animation, huh?

00:23:02.480 --> 00:23:05.070
That's what I've been saying this whole time!

00:23:05.070 --> 00:23:09.320
There might be someone out there dying 
to see the vibrations of a chainsaw.

00:23:10.050 --> 00:23:12.860
I want to see the teeth of 
the chainsaw jump around,

00:23:12.860 --> 00:23:14.660
and those kinds of details 
are how I'll survive.

00:23:15.070 --> 00:23:17.290
Even if most people don't appreciate it,

00:23:17.290 --> 00:23:19.820
I have to do it for myself!

00:23:20.250 --> 00:23:22.890
I have to proclaim "Here I am!"

00:23:22.890 --> 00:23:26.660
to the people who can appreciate 
each individual movement!

00:24:55.970 --> 00:25:00.250
<b>Illustration by Kenji Maeba</b>
